{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01M8Ayp9rsEoqXuvZcbA4JHx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the information I need. Let me plan and execute the Day 5 work:\n\n1. **`SpeechRecognizer.swift`** - Replace stub with real SFSpeechRecognizer + AVAudioEngine\n2. **`AlarmRingView.swift`** - Fix Task cancellation + handle throws\n3. **Create `AudioRecorder.swift`**\n4. **Create `RecordingView.swift`**\n5. **`AlarmListView.swift`** - Add recording button to AlarmCard\n\n\n6. **`RewardView.swift`** - Add confetti animation\n7. **`SunnyWalkerTests.swift`** - Add 2+ new tests\n\nI'll start by adding a mic button to AlarmCard that opens RecordingView as a sheet, then implement RecordingView using `@Bindable` since Alarm is a `@Model` and that's the right approach for SwiftData mutations. Now I'm writing the actual implementation code.\n\nFor `SpeechRecognizer.swift`, I need to handle the case where `SFSpeechRecognizer` might be nil if the locale isn't supported, so I'll use an optional instead of force-unwrapping. I'm also adding `throws` to the interface as the cleaner approach rather than catching internally. There's a potential issue where calling `stop()` twice could cause an assertion failure when removing the audio tap, so I'll add an `isListening` flag to guard against that.\n\nWriting SpeechRecognizer implementation...\n\nNow I need to handle errors in the recognition task callback—if the recognizer can't decode audio, that should be caught. I also need to check the `isFinal` flag to know when recognition is complete.\n\nFor `AlarmRingView.swift`, I need to store the speech task so I can cancel it if the user dismisses the alarm early, and handle any errors thrown by `startListening`. For `RecordingView.swift`, I'll use `@Bindable` to pass the alarm model since it's a SwiftData object, and when recording stops, I'll set `alarm.recordingName` to the alarm's UUID string (without the file extension). Building the AlarmCard layout...\n\nNow I'm planning the RewardView with a confetti overlay and falling star animations, then adding test cases for the audio recorder and speech recognizer initial states.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10699,"cache_read_input_tokens":53313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10699,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3514461e-587c-4525-adfa-cd83cf29b320","uuid":"0d720833-9add-471f-a093-78d024c41146","request_id":"req_011CbaNMbWmquLqtWzmx1rc9"}
